    "quote": "It is worth noting that, for the Bank dataset, we were unable to run (Backurs et al. 2019) as the number of demographic group is 3 (i.e., J > 2).",
    "headline": false
  },
  {
    "id": "C86",
    "figure_or_table": null,
    "metric": "Kleindessner et al. 2019 not run for large-scale datasets",
    "unit": "computational feasibility",
    "reported_value": null,
    "conditions": {
      "method": "Kleindessner et al. 2019",
      "datasets": "Census II, Bank",
      "reason": "computational and memory load"
    },
    "type": "absolute",
    "page": 7,
    "quote": "However, we were unable to run the spectral solution of (Kleindessner et al. 2019) for large-scale Census II data set, and for Bank, due to its computational and memory load (as it requires computing the eigenvalue decomposition of the square affinity matrix).",
    "headline": false
  },
  {
    "id": "C87",
    "figure_or_table": null,
    "metric": "algorithm scales to J>2",
    "unit": "applicability",
    "reported_value": null,
    "conditions": {
      "method": "variational fair clustering",
      "demographics": "J > 2 (e.g., Bank)"
    },
    "type": "trend",
    "page": 7,
    "quote": "Our algorithm scales up to more than two demographic groups, i.e., when J > 2 (e.g., Bank), unlike many of the existing approaches.",
    "headline": true
  },
  {
    "id": "C88",
    "figure_or_table": null,
    "metric": "bound optimizer handles large-scale graph data",
    "unit": "scalability",
    "reported_value": null,
    "conditions": {
      "method": "variational fair clustering",
      "objective": "Ncut",
      "data": "large-scale pairwise graph data"
    },
    "type": "trend",
    "page": 7,
    "quote": "Furthermore, for Ncut graph clustering, our bound optimizer can deal with large-scale data sets, unlike (Kleindessner et al. 2019), which requires eigen decomposition for large affinity matrices.",
    "headline": true
  },
  {
    "id": "C89",
    "figure_or_table": null,
    "metric": "parallel implementation of lambda exploration",
    "unit": "implementation",
    "reported_value": null,
    "conditions": {
