    "quote": "The difference here is that we run independently for each lambda, which can be implemented in parallel.",
    "headline": false
  },
  {
    "id": "C90",
    "figure_or_table": null,
    "metric": "convergence guarantee from MM theory",
    "unit": "theoretical guarantee",
    "reported_value": null,
    "conditions": {
      "method": "variational fair clustering",
      "theory": "MM procedures (Vaida 2005), Theorem 3"
    },
    "type": "trend",
    "page": 4,
    "quote": "Our variational model belongs to the family of MM procedures, whose theoretical guarantees are well-studied in the literature. Theorem 3 in (Vaida 2005) states a condition for convergence of the general MM procedure to a local minimum.",
    "headline": false
  },
  {
    "id": "C91",
    "figure_or_table": null,
    "metric": "auxiliary function strictly convex",
    "unit": "mathematical property",
    "reported_value": null,
    "conditions": {
      "method": "variational fair clustering",
      "auxiliary_function": "sum of linear terms and strictly convex negative entropy"
    },
    "type": "absolute",
    "page": 4,
    "quote": "In our case, the auxiliary function in (11) is strictly convex, as it is the sum of linear terms and a strictly convex term (the negative entropy), and is optimized under affine simplex constraints.",
    "headline": false
  },
